# Security Rules

- Never hardcode Spotify Client Secret or access tokens in source files.
- Store all secrets in environment variables only (`SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET`, `SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID`, etc.).
- Use HttpOnly cookies for storing Spotify access/refresh tokens on the client.
- Do not expose refresh tokens in API responses, logs, or client-side state.
- If a secret appears to be leaked, immediately tell the user to regenerate it in the Spotify Dashboard.
- Keep `.env*` files out of git; provide `.env.example` templates only.
